description:
Project Overview

We are Craft Coffee & Pastry, a premium 100% gluten-free bakery in the Netherlands with three physical bakery locations in Amsterdam, Almere and Arnhem, as well as an established WooCommerce webshop.

We are looking for an experienced senior WordPress/WooCommerce developer or specialized agency to completely redesign and rebuild the frontend of our existing website while preserving and optimizing the existing WooCommerce ecosystem.

This is not a new webshop built from scratch.

Our current website is an operational WordPress/WooCommerce environment containing existing products, customers, orders, SEO value, payment integrations, shipping/pickup functionality and several business-critical plugins.

The objective is to transform it into a:

premium, international, cinematic, extremely fast, mobile-first bakery and e-commerce experience.

Think less “standard WooCommerce website” and more premium international food/fashion/lifestyle brand, while retaining the reliability and manageability of WordPress/WooCommerce.

Approximately 75% of our website traffic is mobile, so mobile UX is critical.

⸻

About Craft

Craft Coffee & Pastry is a specialist gluten-free bakery, but we deliberately do not position ourselves as a medical/dietary webshop.

Our positioning is:

A premium bakery that happens to be 100% gluten-free.

Our croissants are our hero product and the main reason customers travel to us.

Amsterdam is our international flagship location and receives customers from around the world. Arnhem also has growth potential with customers from the Netherlands and nearby Germany, while Almere combines retail with an important part of our production.

The new website should communicate craftsmanship, exclusivity and product quality while simultaneously making it extremely easy to:

order online, order for pickup, discover our bakery locations and understand why Craft is different.

Our preferred brand direction can be summarized as:

Luxury Editorial Bakery

with:

* large cinematic food photography;
* generous whitespace;
* sophisticated typography;
* minimal but intuitive navigation;
* subtle, smooth animations;
* strong product storytelling;
* premium editorial layouts;
* excellent mobile UX;
* very fast performance.

The site should feel international and premium rather than like a typical WordPress bakery website.

⸻

Current Technical Environment

The existing website uses:

* WordPress
* WooCommerce
* Astra theme
* Elementor
* Elementor Pro
* Mollie
* MyParcel
* pickup/delivery date functionality
* minimum/maximum quantity functionality
* PDF invoicing
* MailPoet
* SEOPress
* Google/analytics integrations
* several additional operational and optimization plugins

The current site works, but our main frustrations are:

* slow performance;
* too many plugins;
* possible overlapping/conflicting plugins;
* Elementor overhead;
* difficult maintenance;
* too many clicks in important customer journeys;
* mediocre mobile experience;
* insufficient premium brand appearance.

We do not want to throw away the WooCommerce infrastructure that already works.

We want to replace and improve the presentation layer and clean up/optimize the underlying WordPress environment.

⸻

Required Technical Approach

We are looking for a developer/team capable of building a custom lightweight WordPress theme, preferably using native WordPress/Gutenberg functionality and ACF or an equally lightweight and maintainable architecture.

We specifically do NOT want:

* Elementor
* Elementor Pro
* Divi
* WPBakery
* another heavy page builder
* an off-the-shelf ThemeForest/theme template
* a prebuilt theme merely customized with our colors and fonts
* unnecessary JavaScript/CSS libraries
* unnecessary plugins

The finished website should no longer depend on Astra, Elementor or Elementor Pro.

We expect clean, maintainable and documented code.

⸻

Existing WooCommerce Environment Must Be Preserved

This is critical.

The rebuild must preserve, where applicable:

* all products;
* product variations;
* existing customers/accounts;
* existing orders and order history;
* WooCommerce settings;
* payment workflows;
* Mollie;
* shipping functionality;
* MyParcel;
* store pickup;
* delivery/pickup date selection;
* minimum/maximum quantities;
* PDF invoicing;
* transactional emails;
* analytics/tracking;
* existing SEO value;
* important existing URLs;
* metadata;
* redirects where required.

We do not want functionality rebuilt unnecessarily when the existing solution works correctly.

However, the selected developer must be capable of auditing the existing plugin stack.

We want unnecessary, duplicate, conflicting or performance-heavy plugins identified and, where appropriate, safely removed, replaced or consolidated without losing required functionality.

⸻

Design / UI/UX

We already have:

* a detailed project brief;
* wireframes;
* a clearly defined brand/design direction;
* an interactive frontend prototype showing one possible interpretation of the concept.

The existing prototype is a reference, not something that must simply be copied.

We would like the selected designer/developer to improve upon it where possible.

We are particularly interested in candidates who can combine strong UI/UX design with serious WooCommerce engineering.

Before full development begins, we expect the principal layouts to be designed and approved in Figma, including dedicated mobile designs.

⸻

Approximately 10 Unique Page Designs / Templates

We expect approximately 10 unique page designs/templates.

This does not mean every content page needs an individual design. Reusable templates should be used intelligently.

1. Homepage

Premium editorial homepage with strong visual storytelling, hero products, craftsmanship, social proof, webshop conversion and bakery locations.

2. Shop / Product Category

Main webshop and product category experience.

Examples include:

* Croissants
* Bread
* Pastry
* other bakery products

3. Single Product Page

A premium WooCommerce product template optimized for mobile conversion.

4. Bakery / Location Page

One reusable design system/template for:

* Amsterdam
* Almere
* Arnhem

with location-specific content, photography, opening hours, directions and relevant calls to action.

5. Pickup & Delivery

Clear explanation and customer journey for:

* store pickup;
* shipping within the Netherlands;
* shipping to Belgium;
* shipping to Germany.

6. Craftsmanship / Our Story

Editorial storytelling around our bakery, products and craftsmanship.

7. Allergen / Product Finder

Interactive allergen/product information with filtering/search functionality.

8. Business / Wholesale

B2B/professional customer page.

9. Contact / Standard Content

Reusable structure for simpler informational pages.

10. Cart / Checkout / My Account

The e-commerce journey must remain visually consistent with the premium website.

We do not want the customer to experience a beautiful premium website and suddenly arrive at a generic-looking WooCommerce cart or checkout.

⸻

Mobile-First Requirement

Approximately 75% of our visitors use mobile devices.

Mobile cannot therefore be an afterthought.

At minimum, we expect explicit mobile UI/UX designs for:

* Homepage
* Shop/category
* Product page
* Bakery/location
* Allergen/Product Finder
* Cart
* Checkout

The objective is not merely “responsive”.

The mobile experience should be deliberately designed for speed, usability and conversion.

⸻

Languages

The website must support:

* Dutch
* English
* German

The multilingual architecture must be implemented correctly from the start, including SEO considerations.

⸻

Performance

Performance is one of the main reasons for this redevelopment.

We expect a performance-focused architecture and attention to:

* Core Web Vitals;
* mobile performance;
* image optimization;
* modern image formats;
* lazy loading where appropriate;
* efficient CSS/JS;
* minimizing render-blocking resources;
* sensible caching;
* database/plugin overhead;
* WooCommerce-specific performance considerations.

We understand that third-party services can affect absolute PageSpeed scores, so we are not asking for meaningless promises of “100/100”.

We are asking for a demonstrably fast, technically sound website.

⸻

SEO & Migration

The existing site has established search visibility.

The redesign must therefore be SEO-safe.

This includes:

* preserving important URLs wherever possible;
* mapping changed URLs;
* proper 301 redirects;
* preserving relevant metadata;
* correct canonical handling;
* multilingual SEO;
* structured data where appropriate;
* sitemap/indexation checks;
* avoiding broken links;
* avoiding accidental loss of indexed pages.

Organic visibility must not be sacrificed for the redesign.

⸻

Staging, Testing & Deployment

All development must take place in a staging environment.

The existing production website must remain operational until the replacement has been fully tested and approved.

Before launch we expect complete regression testing of important workflows, including:

* add to cart;
* cart;
* checkout;
* Mollie payment;
* pickup;
* shipping;
* pickup/delivery date;
* minimum/maximum quantities;
* customer account;
* order emails;
* invoices;
* MyParcel workflow;
* multilingual pages;
* mobile devices;
* tablet;
* desktop.

A complete backup and rollback procedure must exist before deployment.

⸻

Post-Launch

Please include a period of post-launch technical support in your proposal.

We expect any bugs resulting from the redevelopment/migration to be resolved as part of the project rather than charged as new development immediately after launch.

Please specify your proposed support period.

⸻

Ownership & Vendor Lock-In

After final payment, Craft Coffee & Pastry must have full ownership/access to:

* custom theme/source code;
* custom plugins/code developed specifically for the project;
* Figma files;
* design assets created for the project;
* WordPress administrator access;
* hosting/server deployment;
* documentation.

The website must not depend on a developer-owned account, proprietary license or private platform in order to continue functioning.

We must be able to appoint another qualified WordPress developer in the future if necessary.

⸻

Deliverables

The project should include:

* technical audit of existing WordPress/WooCommerce installation;
* plugin audit;
* final technical architecture;
* UI/UX design in Figma;
* desktop and mobile designs;
* approximately 10 unique templates;
* custom lightweight WordPress theme;
* custom WooCommerce frontend;
* migration/integration with existing WooCommerce environment;
* multilingual implementation;
* plugin cleanup/optimization;
* performance optimization;
* SEO-safe migration;
* staging environment;
* cross-device/browser QA;
* WooCommerce regression testing;
* production deployment;
* documentation/handover;
* post-launch support.

⸻

Who We Are Looking For

We are not looking for the cheapest WordPress freelancer.

We are looking for someone who can demonstrate excellent value and who has successfully completed comparable production projects.

Ideal candidates will have demonstrable experience with:

* advanced WooCommerce;
* custom WordPress theme development;
* existing-store migrations/rebuilds;
* custom WooCommerce templates;
* checkout/cart customization;
* performance optimization;
* plugin audits;
* multilingual WooCommerce;
* technical SEO migrations;
* mobile-first UI/UX;
* Figma;
* staging and production deployment.

Experience with premium food, hospitality, fashion, beauty or lifestyle brands is a plus.

Both experienced individual senior developers and specialized agencies are welcome to apply.

⸻

IMPORTANT: Portfolio Requirements

Please do not send us:

* demo websites;
* speculative redesigns;
* Figma concepts presented as client work;
* ThemeForest templates;
* websites where your role cannot be explained.

We have already encountered this during our selection process.

Instead, please send 3–5 LIVE production WordPress/WooCommerce websites that you or your agency actually developed.

For each example, tell us:

1. What exactly did you do?
UI/UX, Figma, custom theme, WooCommerce, backend, integrations, performance, migration, etc.

2. Was it a new build or a rebuild of an existing WooCommerce website?

3. Is the version we are looking at today substantially the work your team delivered?

We may independently inspect the technical implementation of shortlisted portfolio examples.

⸻

Budget

We are currently receiving proposals from several international developers/agencies.

For reference, proposals received so far for the complete project are approximately in the €3,500–€5,000 range, depending on scope and experience.

We are therefore considering a fixed-price budget in approximately this range.

However, this is not a race to the lowest price.

We are willing to consider a higher proposal if you can clearly demonstrate why your technical expertise, design quality, process or deliverables justify the additional investment.

Please submit your actual fixed-price proposal for the complete scope rather than automatically matching our indicated budget.

⸻

Proposed Project Structure / Milestones

Our preferred structure is approximately:

Milestone 1 — 10%
Technical audit, plugin audit, architecture, staging setup and confirmed implementation plan.

Milestone 2 — 20%
Approved Figma UI/UX designs for desktop and mobile.

Milestone 3 — 25%
Custom WordPress theme and principal page templates implemented on staging.

Milestone 4 — 25%
WooCommerce integration, multilingual implementation, plugin optimization and all major functionality operational on staging.

Milestone 5 — 20%
Complete QA, performance/SEO checks, regression testing, deployment, handover and agreed post-launch support.

The final milestone structure can be discussed with the selected candidate.
